;; A Java forms program calling classes it names only at run time (A6 of the Ghidra case study's G1 plan;
;; J2G-SPEC §4.1, "Roots from a program's metadata"): rm.Plugin is named by a resource and listed in the
;; jar's native-image reflect-config.json, so j2g roots its constructor and run(); rm.Constant is named by
;; a constant string at a Class.forName site and by a class literal's getMethod("hello"), which j2g roots;
;; rm.Unlisted is named only at run time, so it is not in the program (:roots :entry: no class of the
;; program is rooted wholesale). rm.Lazy (A18) is found by Class.forName(name, false, loader) without its initializer
;; running, which runs at its constructor (rooted by its class literal's getConstructor).
{:main-class rm.Main :roots :entry}
